    "answer": "PostgreSQL pgvector is used as a vector store backend in SimpleMem via the VectorStoreBackend protocol. It requires PostgreSQL ≥ 15 with the pgvector extension (created via `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector`), and uses a `vector(1024)` column with an HNSW index on `vec vector_cosine_ops`. Semantic search uses the `<=>` cosine operator with `ScoreOrder.ASCENDING` (lower distance = better), keyword search uses case-insensitive `ILIKE`, and structured search uses parameterized `::jsonb @> ::jsonb`. It is enabled by setting `STORAGE_BACKEND=pgvector` (with `PG_DSN`), and LanceDB remains the default backend. Text columns use `VARCHAR(N)` rather than `TEXT` for broad compatibility. The backend implements insert, semantic_search, keyword_search, structured_search, count, get_all, optimize, and clear, uses thread-local connections, and is schema-bootstrap idempotent. It can also connect to InterSystems IRIS via iris-pgwire ≥ 1.7.3 without code changes, only by pointing PG_DSN at the pgwire endpoint.",
    "uncertainty": "Low. All claims are directly supported by the supplied SimpleMem pull request evidence. The iris-pgwire details (≥ 1.7.3, no code changes, DSN-only switch) are drawn from the provided text.",
